  "body": "This makes validated selective Cells the default for **calling-thread decoding**: `BzReader::new/with_kernels`, `decode` and `decode_blocks`. Cells retains its exact admission, budgets and Segmented refusal/fallback. Explicit parallel APIs (including one worker), cooperative/team decoding, `Scratch`'s omitted type parameter and `decode_with::<Segmented>` remain unchanged. Python resolved-one-thread calls follow the new sequential defaults; explicit zero resolves to one, while None uses available parallelism.\n\nThe kernel is PR #380 at a8a23c11607864cb431f87fff38169e10c41685f with exactly three documentation-line changes. No executable kernel, unsafe invariant, writer, induction or allocation change. [Entry-point map, source correspondence, safety argument and historical i9 evidence](https://github.com/lmmx/mibz2/blob/a9c7716aaf664a7898f3d8f37c955e09d5204a23/docs/journal/2026-11-14-cells-default/INTEGRATION.md).\n\n**Actual-default CI result: reviewable, not merge-qualified.** First/only paired [run43534513477](https://github.com/lmmx/mibz2/actions/runs/43534513477), exact head a9c7716aaf664a7898f3d8f37c955e09d5204a23 versus master6dec95ba6aaf59d5134e5ab119fd52433e2032ee, AMD EPYC7763, Rust1.100.0, ten paired rounds:\n\n| One-thread corpus | Wall change [95% CI] | CPU change | Peak RSS change |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Wikidata | −0.8% [−3.1%, +1.7%] | −0.8% | +30.9% |\n| text | −1.0% [−3.3%, +1.4%] | −1.0% | +0.0% |\n| pattern | **+59.6% [+57.9%, +61.3%]** | +56.0% | +14.1% |\n| onebyte | **+8.0% [+7.2%, +8.9%]** | +7.3% | +7.3% |\n| random | +0.1% [−0.4%, +0.6%] | +0.2% | −0.0% |\n| records | −0.1% [−1.3%, +1.1%] | −0.1% | −0.1% |\n| runs | +0.1% [−1.0%, +1.1%] | +0.3% | −0.1% |\n\nNo primary or parallel wall regression is established. Text4t improves3.9% [0.6%,7.0%] with unchanged parallel source; this is not attributed to Cells. Every one of420 rows is retained, with full pair/schedule/byte-hash checks and63 intervals exactly reproduced. The [raw archive, complete21-cell table and validation logs](https://github.com/lmmx/mibz2/tree/aa9d2cbaaba2e555d7eadc9f5855c107cf062595/state/reports/cells-default-20261114) preserve adverse findings. CI's standard text corpus differs from the pinned i9 text; no recipe changed. Its separate Segmented phases table is not Cells stage attribution.\n\nThe earlier matched i9 diagnostic remains valid: Wikidata selective/Segmented .8630 [.8319,.8952], selective/original .9256 [.8823,.9711], pattern+43.5%, WikiRSS+31.1%, patternRSS+15.1%. **That experiment did not measure this new public-default build.** Historical #380 default4t failure remains recorded; this PR does not explain its cause.\n\nValidation: Rust1.100 formatting/full Clippy;109 library+70 integration+1doc and27 harness tests; all7 pinned public `decode`/`BzReader`/`decode_blocks` full-byte comparisons against Segmented and libbzip2; all7 relevant local Miri tests including public admission/periodic reach and F01 writer;3 compiled selective mutations killed;28,369 forced Cells and6,152 mixed/default fuzz cases with zero failures. Native/Python/platform packaging/Occupancy/hosted pre-commit CI pass; **full CI Miri still pending**.\n\n[Independent Guardian D105](https://github.com/lmmx/mibz2/blob/13b01b9905f732821c0db3e5efaaa3f20e468d2a/state/reports/D105-public-cells-integration.md) gives scoped PROCEED for caller/lifetime/error/fallback design, carrying native Researcher B5 closure6857443323. Its execution snapshot was partial; completed logs are supplied for Coordinator reconciliation without another full review. Nonblocking malformed-range/selection coverage limits remain explicit. Reused Cells memory is max prior arena request plus4×max position count, plus coexisting fallback/outer/output buffers; concurrent calling-thread users multiply costs.\n\n**Remaining decisions:** #145/6775049636's default-adoption gate remains unmet. Pattern>10% needs Louis's explicit sign-off; onebyte8% also fails the5–10% tier because no ≥16% primary gain at1t exists on this runner. The strict+10%RSS and Wiki1t-gain conditions also fail. Any prospective adoption exception must explicitly address these actual-default results through the established decision/review process; historical failures are not relabelled. Actual-default i9 confirmation before release needs separate registration/authorisation. No workstation run, retry, merge, release, acceptance-policy change or parallel redesign is part of this PR.",
